# Single source of truth for toolchain versions (requirement: reliability).
#
# CI, Docker images, local dev and pre-commit checks all read the pinned values
# from this file (or mirror them in .github/ci/toolchain.lock.env, which
# ci-self-check verifies). One version bump = one commit.
#
# We deliberately use the *release line* rather than "latest". An unpinned
# toolchain makes CI nondeterministic: the same commit can pass on Monday and
# fail on Wednesday because a toolchain was released overnight, which destroys
# the "same code, same result" property this POC is meant to measure.
